      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TASSIE POWER (1) has been steady in 2 starts this season at Hobart, and is normally hitting his straps at about this time of his prep. He meets a small field in a very winnable race here, and he goes on top of our selections. OXIDIZE (5) was a bold runner-up when resuming in a tougher class here at the end of October, and then was a touch plain in fourth place at this level 2 weeks ago. She may be looking for more ground than 1200m, but the field size suits her, and she can take this out. PLATINUM REGGAE (6) has been building her fitness, and her last start was her best this term when fifth, just over a length from the winner. She faces another small field, and is ready now to put her best hoof forward. GET 'EM WARRIOR (3) is another who will be close to full fitness after a couple of solid efforts back from a spell. The pole position enhances his top 3 claims. EASTCOAST MISS (2) likes it here and is worth another chance after a pair of recent modest runs at Hobart.",
